# Code review standards

Orchestration: [orchestration.mdc](orchestration.mdc). When to skip vs run: [reviewer-defaults.mdc](reviewer-defaults.mdc).

## Purpose

Catch real bugs and trust-boundary mistakes - not process theater. Prefer **skip** or **one light specialist** over a heavy general code review.

**Independence:** When a harness review file is written, **one subagent** owns it. Generator must not pre-fill reviewer files.

## When review is warranted

- **Skip:** Direct track, micro-S, docs-only, many S Features (parent/generator verify is enough).
- **Run light `code-reviewer`:** M+ general code, or S when risk is unclear.
- **Run specialist instead/alongside:** auth → security; API → api-reviewer; DB → database-reviewer; UI contract → frontend-evaluator.

Do **not** stack `code-reviewer` + specialist for the same concern “just in case.”

## Quick checklist (when reviewing)

- Diff matches intent; no drive-by refactors.
- New behavior has tests where it matters.
- No secrets; trust boundaries respected if touched.

## Subagents

| Subagent | Use for | Output |
|--|-|--|
| **code-reviewer** | Optional light quality/gates on M+ diffs | `code-review-i<i>.md` |
| **api-reviewer** | HTTP/CLI contracts | `api-review-i<i>.md` |
| **mcp-reviewer** | MCP tools/schemas | `mcp-review-i<i>.md` |
| **security-reviewer** | OWASP, secrets, trust | `security-review-i<i>.md` |
| **database-reviewer** | Migrations, SQL, RLS | `database-review-i<i>.md` |
| **frontend-evaluator** | Live UI vs HTML wireframe | `frontend-eval-i<i>.md` |
| **performance-evaluator** | Perf budgets | `performance-eval-i<i>.md` |
| **doc-updater** | User docs after PASS (if needed) | `docs-review-i<i>.md` |

## Severity

| Level | Action |
|-|--|
| **CRITICAL** / **HIGH** | **BLOCK** |
| **MEDIUM** / **LOW** | Optional note (≤2) or omit - do not block |

## Approval

- **PASS** - no CRITICAL/HIGH (or no review required and gates green)
- **BLOCK** - CRITICAL/HIGH present
